 ```
 
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["home"] }`.
+`tags` is an array of strings sorted alphabetically, `[]` when the task has none.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones; `?tag=home` keeps the tasks with this tag (normalized like the tags below; an invalid or unknown tag lists nothing); `done` and `tag` combine | 200, an array of tasks |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…", "tags": ["home"] }` (`tags` is optional) | 201, the task, or 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
-| `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title`, `done` and / or `tags`; `tags` replaces the whole list (`[]` removes them all), without `tags` they stay as they are | 200, the task, 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }`, or 404 |
+| `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task and its links to tags | 204, or 404 |
+| `GET /api/tags` | Lists the tags in use with their number of tasks, sorted by name: `[{ "name": "home", "count": 2 }]`; a tag no task uses is not listed | 200, an array |
+
+### Tags
+
+Each tag is trimmed and lowercased, and duplicates are removed. A valid tag is 1 to 30 characters among `a-z`, `0-9`
+and `-`, and a task has at most 10 tags. `tags` must be an array of strings (`null`, a string or an empty tag is invalid).
+Otherwise the request answers `400` with `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` and nothing changes (a rejected POST creates no
+task).
 
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
 ## Layout
 
-- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
+- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied). Tables: `tasks`;
+  `tags` (`id`, `name` unique); `task_tags` (`task_id`, `tag_id`, both `ON DELETE CASCADE`: deleting a task removes its links).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
 - `public/`: the page.
 - `test/`: the API tests, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
